The '''Chest''' is one of five final levels in The Binding of Isaac, alongside the {{s|Dark Room}}, {{s|The Void}}, the {{s|Corpse}}, and {{s|Home}}.

The Chest can be accessed with three methods: Touching the chest dropped by {{e|Isaac}} while having {{i|The Polaroid}} (always dropped by {{e|Mom}} after beating Isaac five times) equipped, or, while in the {{s|Cathedral}}, by using Telepills or another item that acts like [[Telepills]], and being sent to the {{r|I AM ERROR}} room, or finding a {{r|Black Market}} on the Cathedral and going into the beam of light.

Like the Cathedral before it, the Chest consists of only one floor. In the Chest, it is not possible to bomb doors open to skip rooms. The Chest's rooms are usually devoid of [[Rock]]s and other obstacles and are mainly filled with [[boss]]es and [[mini-boss]]es. The boss of the floor is always {{e|???}}.

The first room in the Chest will automatically contain 4 {{E|Locked Chest}}s. These special chests always contain [[Treasure Room (Item Pool)|Treasure Room items]]. Rarely, these chests can also be {{e|Mega Chest}}s or {{e|Eternal Chest}}s. Additionally, all {{e|Chest}}s, {{e|Bomb Chest}}s, and {{e|Locked Chest}}s spawned in the Chest will always contain Treasure Room Items. This means that a lot of different items can be found in the Chest when clearing rooms with items or effects that raise the chance of spawning chests. This can be useful when trying to complete the [[collection page]]. {{dlc|nr}} Destroying {{m|Slot Machine}}s, {{m|Fortune Telling Machine}}s, and all types of {{m|Beggar}}s with the exception of the {{m|Shell Game}} will also spawn items.

After completing the Chest or the Dark Room for the first time, the first room of the Chest will always contain a large golden door, which can be unlocked with either the Key Pieces (combination of {{i|Key Piece 1}} and {{i|Key Piece 2}}), {{i|Dad's Key}}, {{p|Get out of Jail Free Card}}, or {{i|Mr. ME!}}, allowing access to {{e|Mega Satan}}.

